    ("3.4", "Origin and destination correct on all BOLs", "Flag", "All 12 BOLs ship from 'BioEnergie AE Côte-Nord Canada, 175 Portage des Mousses, Port-Cartier, Québec G5B 2V9' to SOPOR Baie-Comeau, carrier Transport Baie-Comeau; the rail leg is Watco (COBB Loads tab). Two naming gaps on the new leg: the guidance, the Certify components and Ops M10 call the transload 'Baton Rouge', while the only route evidence names 'RailLogix (Carville LA)' with origin 6045 Point Clair Rd, Carville, LA 70721; and the Basco end of that map is 4675 LA-115, St Landry, while the Opelousas map ends at 4687 LA-115. [log:bols.per_bol, cobb.loads_tab, vvb_guidance.quote_br_change, route_evidence, certify.certify_sources_enumeration]", "PDD Sec A"),
    ("3.5", "Transportation distances consistent with known AECN routes and evidenced", "Fail", "(1) Baton Rouge rail: Certify 'Distance traveled' reads 2,153 km with no source. Ops K10 holds 2152 under 'Rail (mi)', the guidance gives 'Rail distance from the loading origin to Baton Rouge: 2,152 (map evidence is added in drive)', and the September GHG Statement Report v1.7 states 'Its rail leg (2,152 mi)'. 2,153 km is 1,337.8 mi, about 61 % of Watco's 2,199 mi to Opelousas. On 2,152 mi the leg is 4.306208 t against Certify's 2.676997 t, understated by 1.629211 t. Four Drive searches on 2026-10-07 (titles; full text '2,152' and '2152 mi'; and Certify's own figure '2153' or '2,153', whose 50 results hold it only as BOL '2153-T' and in no distance), the W4 folder, the Rail Logix Lessons Learned document and the 72 Certify sources hold no SOPOR-Baton Rouge rail distance record. (2) Baton Rouge truck: 136 mi agrees with the guidance and is the longest of the three routes on the map in the W4 Drive root (121 / 117 / 136 mi), as the statement report's longest-route rule requires, but the map is not linked in Certify. (3) The rail allocated distance is round trip this week: Ops M42 15,102.68824 mi (2 x 2,152 + 2 x 2,199 + 2 x 2,199 + 2 x 2,199 x SHPX215079's share) against one way in W1-W3 and in the 2026-10-01 Ops copy (7,551.34412 mi), so W4 charges 0.235078 t more than the September weeks before it; the guidance names the round trip for the tanker leg only. The railcar factor is 'Embodied Emissions per Mile Traveled (MTCO2e)' with no empty-return uplift, so the round trip fits it and the one-way basis of W1-W3 charged fewer miles than the railcars travelled; the basis needs settling for the period, not W4 reverting to one way. SHPX215079 now carries 3,200.34412 mi across W2 (one way) and W4 (round trip), neither basis for the railcar. (4) 'Allocated Distance AECN to Sopor Quebec (truck)' 1,111.70083 mi follows the Ops method on 107.49722 mi, not the attached-sheet L42 1,111.729637 (effect -0.0000068 t); it is linked to four Mangrove maps of the AECN-to-Opelousas road route (3,672.1 km) and not to the Ops Notes that holds the allocation. (5) 'Allocated Distance Opelousas to B6 (truck)' 1,946 mi (42.9 x 2 x 10 + 136 x 2 x 4) has no source. (6) The Watco email names no railcar, route or date. AECN-SOPOR 107.49722 mi (173 km map) and Opelousas-Basco 42.9 mi reproduce. [log:certify.components, certify.modal_reads, ops_notes.railcars, ops_notes.rollup, vvb_guidance.quote_br_values, vvb_guidance.quote_br_method, rp_status.statement_report_v1_7, route_evidence, certify.presence_checks.baton_rouge_route_evidence, certify.sources_downloaded_and_opened, certify.ops_notes_copies, prior_weeks.w2_SHPX215079, certify.attachment_map, route_evidence.search_2153, standard_efs.railcar_embodied_build, recompute.findings]", "Transport Emissions Acctg v1.1"),
    ("3.6", "Transport mode matches oil type and route", "Pass", "Eight transport components: AECN-to-SOPOR tanker truck (process + embodied), SOPOR-to-Opelousas rail (process) and SOPOR-to-Baton Rouge rail (process) with one shared rail embodied component, Opelousas-to-Basco and Baton Rouge-to-Basco tanker truck (process) with one shared truck embodied component. [log:certify.components]", "Certify Datapoints"),
    ("3.7", "Billing documents present and consistent with BOL", "Flag", "Each BOL package bundles the Straight BOL, Shipping Details, the BioEnergie weigh ticket, the TSCA certificate and a Charm PO; all 12 read, and each weigh-ticket 'Masse nette' equals the BOL delivered mass. Hygiene: the page-5 PO is Q42025 of 10/2/2025 (line 'Q32025', Ship To El Dorado, KS; 1.5) with the seller signature blank on 8 of the 12 (2497-R, 2498-R, 2500-R, 2461-R, 2465-R, 2466-R, 2467-R, 2453-R); 2466-R is a corrected package ('***Correction of density and final liters', density 1.1980 and litres 21,586 hand-corrected; masses unchanged); 2498-R prints CofA 'RS2-260825-1' on page 1 and 'RS2-260828-1' on Shipping Details; 2453-R prints production period '#0X-2026'. [log:bols.per_bol, bols.po_page, bols.hygiene]", "VR App. 1"),

    ("SECTION", "4. Bio-Oil Composition & Testing", "", "", ""),
    ("4.1", "CHN analysis PDF present", "Pass", "SGS Certificate of Analysis SR26-05719.002 (SGS order 5506143), page 2 of the three-page report in Drive Testing/, read this session. It is not linked to 'Carbon Content of Bio-oil Injected (per injection)' in Certify (9.10). [log:lab_results, drive_folder.testing, certify.presence_checks.sgs_certificate, certify.attachment_gate]", "VR App. 1"),
    ("4.2", "Carbon content within expected AECN range", "Pass", f"Carbon 44.0 % (m/m), marked '#' ('Result is outside of test method limits and/or analytical range used in method precision study'). MRV_AECN_Analysis.xlsx Summary Statistics (opened this session): mean {cr['mean_C_pct']} %, SD {cr['sd_C_pct']} %, n {cr['n']}, so the two-SD band is {cr['lower_2sd']:.2f} % to {cr['upper_2sd']:.2f} %; the batch sits {Z:.3f} SD above the mean. Ops Summary E17 0.44 and Certify Carbon Content 44 % match. W3 read 39.7 %. [log:lab_results.carbon_pct, lab_results.hash_footnote, lab_results.w3_comparison, carbon_range, ops_notes.summary_aecn, certify.components, _derived_values.carbon_z_calc]", "Biomass Feedstock Acctg v1.2"),
    ("4.3", "Hydrogen and nitrogen values reported and reasonable", "Pass", f"Hydrogen 6.6 % (marked '#'; dataset mean {cr['h_mean_pct']} %, SD {cr['h_sd_pct']} %); Nitrogen '<0.75' % (m/m), below the reporting limit. [log:lab_results.hydrogen_pct, lab_results.nitrogen_pct, carbon_range]", "Biomass Feedstock Acctg v1.2"),
    ("4.4", "Lab report references correct batch/sample ID", "Flag", "CLIENT ID '9-2026-W4-AECN', SAMPLED 25-Sep-2026 14:00 (Ops Summary D17 2026-09-25, C17 'SR26-05719.002'), RECEIVED 28-Sep-2026, report 28-Sep-2026: the identity ties. The LOCATION field prints 'FORT LUPTON, CO' on the AECN page while the AECN composite is drawn at Basco, Louisiana; W3's certificate printed the same location. [log:lab_results.client_id, lab_results.sampled, lab_results.received, lab_results.location_on_certificate, ops_notes.summary_aecn]", "VR Sec 5.1"),
