    ("SECTION", "5. Ops Notes Accuracy & Internal Consistency", "", "", ""),
    ("5.1", "Correct batch ID and injection week in Ops Notes", "Flag", "'AECN Rail'!B2 reads INJ-09-2026-W4, week 2026-09-18 to 2026-09-25; all 14 offload rows dated 2026-09-25; Certify period 2026-09-19 to 2026-09-25, inside the guidance's W4 window '18 – 25 September 2026'. Label error carried from W3: A3/A4 read 'Week Start (Sat)' and 'Week End (Sat)' but 2026-09-18 and 2026-09-25 are Fridays, and 2026-09-18 is also W3's end date (no offload is booked in both weeks). [log:ops_notes.batch_id_cell, ops_notes.week_start, ops_notes.week_end, ops_notes.week_labels, ops_notes.offload_table, certify.removal_period, vvb_guidance.quote_br_scope]", "verify header"),
    ("5.2", "Scale ticket values correctly transcribed into Ops Notes", "Flag", "Ops D/E equal the 28 ticket gross weights exactly (recompute section 1). Ticket labels are inconsistent: both SHPX215039 offload 2 tickets (1124426261598, 1312226261663) carry commodity 'SHPX215039 O1', the label of offload 1; SHPX215053 offload 4's empty ticket 1186426267016 reads 'SHPX215053' with no offload number; SHPX215053 labels vary ('SHPX215053 01', 'SHPX 215053 OFF 2', 'SHPX215053 O3'); the four SHPX215079 tickets print no delivery site. [log:scale_tickets.label_notes, scale_tickets.offloads, recompute.lines]", "VR Sec 5.1"),
    ("5.3", "Oil and aqueous phase mass reconciliation", "N/A", "AECN-only removal, no aqueous phase. [log:oil_type]", ""),
    ("5.4", "COBB values present and match Ops Notes/Certify", "Pass", "COBB tab 'Basco Injection -- COBB' rows 3724-3737 (latest import 2026-10-05 12:24:22), column A 'INJ-09-2026-W4_bio_oil' confirmed before reading: all 14 offloaded_quantity_kg equal the Ops delivered masses (mass-chain cobb_offload_consistency 14 of 14 PASS), offload 4 of SHPX215079 at the cut 14,321.76 kg; origin_quantity_kg equals each railcar's BOL total (77,570 / 77,640 / 77,770 / 77,870); BOL_number lists each railcar's three BOLs; injection_completion_date 2026-09-25. [log:cobb.tab, cobb.row_id_at_qa, cobb.batch_id_col_a, cobb.offloaded_quantity_kg, cobb.origin_quantity_kg, mass_chain.counts]", "COBB tracker"),
    ("5.5", "pH measurement noted", "Pass", "pH 2.97 on all 14 offload rows (G28:G41) and in the rollup G46, inside the O6 target '2.0 - 4.0'. The method is recorded as a cell note on AECN Truck H28 and Kerry D18: 'Wellhead pH = weekly median of Ignition PH-1041, gated to StateRun=1; provided by G. Lutz 2026-09-30.' pH is not a Certify datapoint. [log:ops_notes.offload_table, ops_notes.rollup.pH, ops_notes.constants, ops_notes.cell_comments]", "GHG Stmt Sec C"),
    ("5.6", "Completion date present and matches COBB", "Pass", "COBB injection_completion_date 2026-09-25 on all 14 rows; Ops offload rows dated 2026-09-25; Certify period ends 2026-09-25. [log:cobb.injection_completion_date, ops_notes.offload_table, certify.removal_period]", "VR Sec 3.5"),
    ("5.7", "No erroneous density measurements", "N/A", "Density field expected blank for AECN in Ops Notes; the lab density is used only for the safe-injection check (4.6). [log:oil_type]", ""),

    ("SECTION", "6. AECN Feedstock Emissions & Allocation", "", "", ""),
    ("6.1", "AECN process emissions LCA CI spreadsheet present", "Fail", "The vendor workbook 'Bioenergy AE Cote-Nord Canada - LCA CI calculation - 1Jan2026 to 30Jun2026.xlsx' is not in this removal's 72 Certify sources and not in the W4 Drive folder. The pyrolysis-process CI is linked to 'FH 2026 LCA w Stack Emissions.xlsx' only, whose I11 0.133052027800741 is labelled 'From Vendor LCA'; W3's removal carried the vendor workbook on the same datapoint, so the vendor half of 0.13712 has no backing on W4. [log:lca_files, certify.presence_checks.vendor_lca_files, drive_folder.root_items]", "VR App. 1"),
    ("6.2", "LCA with stack emissions file present", "Pass", f"'FH 2026 LCA w Stack Emissions.xlsx' is linked to the pyrolysis-process CI; Sheet1 I12 {L['lca_files']['fh_2026']['I12_total']} (stack I10 {L['lca_files']['fh_2026']['I10_stack']} + vendor I11 {L['lca_files']['fh_2026']['I11_vendor']}). [log:lca_files.fh_2026, certify.attachment_map]", "VR App. 1"),
    ("6.3", "Supporting GHG data file present", "Fail", "'Supporting GHG data 30Jun2026 S.xlsx', linked on W3's removal, is not in this removal's 72 Certify sources and not in the W4 Drive folder. [log:lca_files, certify.presence_checks.vendor_lca_files, drive_folder.root_items]", "VR App. 1"),
    ("6.4", "AECN pyrolysis process EF matches current half-year value", "Pass", f"Certify CI 0.13712 tCO2e/t against Standard EF sheet 2026 tab row 4 '{row4['name']}', Final Quantity {row4['final_F']} (source '{row4['source_G']}'); the removal falls in H2 2026. Certify's value is the sheet value rounded up at the fifth decimal, 0.000769 t more emission (recompute section 5). [log:standard_efs.row4_aecn_process_H2_2026, standard_efs.period_basis, standard_efs._primary_source_opened, recompute.lines]", "Certify Component Inputs"),
    ("6.5", "AECN pyrolysis embodied EF applied", "Pass", f"Certify CI 0.02116 tCO2e/t; Standard EF sheet row 5 Final Quantity {EFS['row5_aecn_embodied']['final_F']}; 'AECN Embodied Emissions Calc Sheet (1).pdf' (linked, opened) gives 0.02115941123. [log:standard_efs.row5_aecn_embodied, standard_efs._primary_source_opened, lca_files, certify.attachment_map]", "Certify Datapoints"),
    ("6.6", "Mass basis for pyrolysis EFs is pre-sparging origin mass", "Pass", f"Both pyrolysis components use 'Bio-Oil Mass - AECN via Rail' {M_T:.5f} t, the 14 delivered masses before sparging (Ops C46, with SHPX215079 offload 4 at its cut mass), as the guidance sets ('calculated on the delivered mass: scale-ticket net mass, less any Uncertainty Adjustment'). The {loss_kg:.5f} kg lost from SHPX215053, SHPX215039 and SHPX215091 is charged its pyrolysis emissions through the separate 'AECN Bio-oil Loss' component (8.2), so all oil that entered custody carries its upstream emissions. [log:certify.components, ops_notes.rollup.mass_used_kg, vvb_guidance.quote_loss_method, vvb_guidance.quote_loss_purpose, policy.custody_rule, ops_notes.railcars]", "Certify Components"),

    ("SECTION", "7. Gross-to-Net Calculation", "", "", ""),
    ("7.1", "Gross CO2e = injectate mass x carbon wt% x 3.667", "Pass", f"{MOI_T:.7f} t x 0.44 x 3.667 gives {G:.6f} t, Certify's Injection sequestration; the mass input equals Ops F46 MOBI and the carbon equals SGS SR26-05719.002 (recompute sections 3 and 5). No R&D removal this week (K46 blank). [log:certify.components, ops_notes.rollup.mobi_kg, ops_notes.rollup.mass_removed_rnd_K46, lab_results.carbon_pct, _derived_values.gross_calc, recompute.lines]", "GHG Stmt Sec E"),
    ("7.2", "Process emissions correctly deducted", "Fail", f"Activities 83.620 t in the Calculation view equal the AECN components {ACTS_AECN:.6f} t (pyrolysis {PYRO:.6f}, transport process {PROC_SUM:.6f}, transport embodied {EMB_SUM:.6f}, loss {cv(LOSS):.3f}) plus the site components {cert['activities_site_t']:.6f} t, and every component recomputes from its own inputs. Two AECN legs are wrong against the evidence: the Baton Rouge rail leg is understated by 1.629211 t (3.5) and the Opelousas truck leg overstated by 0.378688 t (2.7), so activities are understated by 1.250523 t net; on the evidence they are 84.869836 t (recompute CORRECTIONS D). The transport part of this error is offset one-for-one by the BCU while the BCU equals Certify's own process sum, so it does not move the net (9.8). [log:certify.calc_view, certify.components, certify.activities_site_t, _derived_values.activities_calc, recompute.findings]", "GHG Stmt Sec E"),
    ("7.3", "Uncertainty discount correctly applied", "Pass", f"Calculation view: 'Net CO₂e Removed 362.068 t' from Sequestrations 425.691, Adjustments 22.439, Activities 83.620 and Uncertainty Discount 2.443. Re-derived from the component inputs as one combined one-sigma, one term per datapoint: carbon +/- 0.176 % (1.702765 t), injectant mass +/- 1,015.98 kg (1.639263 t), grid electricity +/- 1,271.5038 kWh at the grid factor 0.4630140342 (0.588724 t), Bio-Oil Mass +/- 1,015.98 kg on the four components that share it (0.178274 t), the Opelousas rail and Baton Rouge truck masses, site diesel and gasoline; this reproduces {cert['uncertainty_discount_t']:.10f} t (recompute section 9) on the inputs as entered; the inputs that lack a +/- are carried in 7a.1, {cert['uncertainty_discount_t'] / cv(SEQ) * 100:.2f} % of gross. [log:certify.calc_view, certify.uncertainty_discount_t, recompute.lines, _derived_values.discount_pct_calc]", "Isometric Standard v2.0 S3.7"),
    ("7.4", "Net removals consistent with BCU Quant and GHG Statement", "Flag", "Certify's GHG statements list (read today) ends at '01 Aug 2026 to 31 Aug 2026' (Certificates issued, 11 Sep 2026, 1,746.14 tCO₂e); the September statement is not in Certify yet. Two September drafts sit in Drive ('Additional Documentation', garrett.lutz@), both read this session. The results workbook 'September1-September30_Bio-Oil_GHG_Statement_Results.xlsx' (edited 2026-10-07T07:43:32Z, when the W3 and W4 Kerry rows swapped values; the W4 AECN row and the totals did not change) carries W4 AECN as 263,834.27 kg injected, gross 425.691, process 63.0690, site 20.5500, reductions 22.4390, discount 2.4429 and net 362.07 t, matching Certify to its rounding (recompute section 11). The 'GHG Statement Report v1.7' (dated 10/3/26, modified 2026-10-05T16:07:59Z) does not match that workbook: Section E process 384.65 against 385.33 t, site 20.48 against 20.55 t, reductions 171.95 against 172.66 t, net 1,744.01 against 1,743.96 t; its Section B gives W4 site emissions 20.482 t with Additional Transport 1.084 t, against Certify's 20.550448 t and 1.15242 t. Both drafts carry Certify's W4 AECN process figure 63.069 t, not the evidence figure 64.319388 t (7.2). [log:rp_status, recompute.findings, recompute.lines, certify.components]", "RP BCU Quant.xlsx"),

    ("SECTION", "7a. Per-Component Uncertainty Verification", "", "", ""),
    ("7a.1", "Layer 1 - every component that needs uncertainty has it on the right input", "Fail", "All 13 AECN component windows opened. Injection sequestration shows +/- on carbon and mass; both pyrolysis components, the AECN-SOPOR and Opelousas truck legs, the Opelousas rail leg and the Baton Rouge truck leg show +/- on their mass input; the three embodied components are per-mile with no mass input; the BCU is a constant reduction. 'SOPOR to Baton Rouge Rail Process Emissions' shows 'Mass of load 77,228.57 kg' with no +/-, where the same mass on the Baton Rouge truck leg carries +/- 290.28 kg (4 x 72.57). The uncertainty reference requires it ('72.57 kg per discrete weight'), and leaving it out understates the discount: 2.4428820922 to 2.4429028145 t on today's inputs, 2.442586 to 2.442640 t once the distance and the Opelousas truck mass are corrected (recompute CORRECTIONS B to C). Missing required data is a Fail at any size ('This includes: reporting errors, data mismatches, missing required data, conflicting evidence'); the ~0.001 t allowance applies to matching values, not to a missing input. It belongs in the same edit as the 3.5 distance on that component. The 'AECN Bio-oil Loss' constant also carries none. On the same removal, outside this batch's scope (site-emissions QA): 'Argon Electricity Usage (RECs)' grid use 2,602.43355 kWh carries no +/- although the knowledge base lists 'Electricity → Grid Electricity Usage: 0.02 × Measured Value (2%)' (with it the discount rises by 0.0001189 t), and the procured-power input carries none on either site electricity component against 'Electricity → Procured Power Electricity Usage: 0.02 × Measured Value (2%)'. [log:certify.modal_reads, certify.components, policy.status_rules, policy.kb_electricity_uncertainty, recompute.findings]", "MRV Uncertainty Cheat Sheet"),
    ("7a.2", "Layer 2 - reported +/- matches the expected value", "Pass", "Where present the +/- is right: 1,015.98 kg on the injectant mass and on 'Bio-Oil Mass - AECN via Rail' (14 offload weighings x 72.57 kg), 725.7 kg on the Opelousas rail mass (10 offloads), 290.28 kg on the Baton Rouge truck mass (4 offloads); carbon 0.176 % against 0.004 x 44.0. One outbound weighing per offload (Failure Category 9). [log:certify.modal_reads, certify.components, ops_notes.summary_aecn, ops_notes._primary_source_opened, _derived_values.unc_calc, recompute.lines]", "Isometric Standard S3.7.3"),
    ("7a.3", "Layer 3 - discount present and consistent", "Pass", f"Uncertainty Discount {cert['uncertainty_discount_t']:.10f} t is present in the Calculation view, carried into the net, and reproduces from the per-datapoint inputs (7.3; recompute section 9). Against the September drafts: the results workbook carries 2.4429 t on the W4 AECN row (M10), and its discount column M2:M12 sums to {L['rp_status']['results_workbook']['discount_column_sum_t']} t against the GHG Statement Report v1.7 Section E 'Uncertainty Discounts' 10998.10 kg / 11.00 t; both agree to their rounding (recompute sections 11 and 12). The September statement is not in Certify yet (7.4), and the discount rests on inputs that still lack the Baton Rouge rail +/- (7a.1). [log:certify.uncertainty_discount_t, certify.calc_view, rp_status.results_workbook.discount_column_sum_t, rp_status.statement_report_v1_7.section_e_discount_lines, rp_status, certify.modal_reads, recompute.lines]", "Isometric Standard S3.7.3"),

    ("SECTION", "8. Data Integrity & Anomaly Check", "", "", ""),
    ("8.1", "No unexplained outliers in mass, carbon or calculated values", "Flag", f"Nets run {min(nets):,} to {max(nets):,} lb, full gross {min(fulls):,} to {max(fulls):,} lb, carbon 0.752 SD above the mean. Eight tickets read 0 on the steer axle, all on tractor CH1 with trailer KL720: SHPX215053 offload 4 empty, SHPX215039 offloads 2 and 3 (full and empty), SHPX215091 offload 2 (full and empty) and offload 4 full; every other ticket reads 9,340 to 12,480 lb on the steer. The CH1/KL720 empties weigh 29,240 to 29,640 lb whether or not the steer reads 0 (29,400 and 29,580 lb with a steer reading), and each gross is the sum of its readings, so the nets stand. The SGS acid number is 156 mg KOH/g (marked '#'), against 61 in W2 and 47 in W3; it is not a Certify input, and no note explains the threefold rise. The Kerry sample in the same SGS order 5506143 reads 154 mg KOH/g, also marked '#', and the QOWV sample 36, so the jump shows in two oils from one lab run. [log:scale_tickets.zero_steer_tickets, scale_tickets.zero_steer_rig, scale_tickets.ch1_kl720_empties_lb, lab_results.acid_number_by_week, lab_results.same_order_acid_numbers, lab_results.hash_footnote, _derived_values.ticket_ranges_calc, _derived_values.carbon_z_calc]", "GHG Stmt Sec C"),
